<title>USA: TWA controller resigns.</title>
<headline>TWA controller resigns.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc said Tuesday it named Christine Deister as vice president and controller, replacing Jody Ruth, who resigned.</p>
<p>The carrier also named Michael Lichty as vice president-corporate finance.  He assumes a vacancy created by the promotion of Michael Palumbo to senior vice president and chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Deister is former assistant treasurer of TWA and Lichty most recently was associate general counsel and assistant secretary.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
